The use of sdbusplus::message::object_path is not working and hence std::string is used.

The following won't compile as operator / can't take sdbusplus::message::object_path as the second operand.
`sdbusplus::message::object_path objectPath;
sdbusplus::message::object_path metricObjectPath;
auto path = objectPath / "Metrics" / metricObjectPath;`


The following will compile but results in object path like this `/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/pcie_devices/Nvidia_ConnectX_255/Ports/UP_0/Metrics/_2fpcie_2fl0_5fto_5frecovery_5fcount`.

`sdbusplus::message::object_path objectPath;
sdbusplus::message::object_path metricObjectPath = "/pcie/l0_to_recovery_count";
auto path = objectPath / "Metrics" / metricObjectPath.str;`

